	(text "MPU6050 GY-521 Module\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 256.286 70.612 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2b1d3f02-bf6f-46e8-ab6a-79a2498d80ca")
	)
	(text "OPTIONAL 5V BUCK (only if no ESP32-S3 IO shield MKE-B01)\n2S battery 6.4-8.4V -> 5V for the dev board 5V pin\nU1 AP63205WU-7  5V fixed, 2A\nC1 10uF in | C2 2x22uF out | C3 100nF SW-BST\nL1 4.7uH, >=2.7A, DCR <100mOhm\nEN -> VIN (auto start) | FB -> 5V out\nMotor VM direct from battery, not from this buck\nNo USB while battery is on unless the board has a diode"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.296 157.734 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "45b15cb0-d9d7-4921-a2f9-98a210910cca")
	)
	(text "Button_START_SET_MODE\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.394 181.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "626992ee-a5c6-490a-bb6a-0fd1013cb523")
	)
	(text "**NOTE: INTERNAL PULL-UP CONFIGURATION**\n\n- GPIO18 (BTN_START), GPIO17 (BTN_SET), GPIO16 (BTN_MODE) use the ESP32-S3 internal pull-up resistors.\n- Configure all pins using `pinMode(GPIO_NUM, INPUT_PULLUP)`.\n- No external pull-up resistors are required.\n- Button pressed: LOW (connected to GND).\n- Button released: HIGH (pulled up internally to 3.3V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 86.614 192.278 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.508 0.508)
			)
		)
		(uuid "77d3e1e5-19c3-4bcb-a57f-8db87807eb32")
	)
